Run `$athena:plan-issue` for GitHub issue #{{ issue_number }}.

The issue (the source of truth for requirements), any prior plan, and any prior
`## 🔍 Plan Review` are in the context above. When a prior review is present,
re-plan to address it. If the plan and the repository architecture disagree, run
`$athena:realign` first and plan against the realigned architecture.

{% include "shared/terse_output_directive.j2" %}

Your final message IS the complete plan, as markdown, starting with the
`# Implementation Plan` heading. The pipeline posts it to the issue, so do not
post issue comments yourself and do not return a summary of what you did. Cover
the objective, the approach and its evidence, the files to create and modify
(real paths, `file.py:line` where known), the implementation order, one runnable
verification command per acceptance criterion, and the skills you used. Do not
include diffs. When you re-plan, output the full revised plan and end it with a
short `## Changes from Review` list of the improvements made.

Do not present a measured metric or run result as a deliverable unless a real
run produced it. Plan the command and leave the measured result to a separate
evidence step.
